{"title":"Joseph Thacker (rez0)","url":"https://josephthacker.com/","favicon":"https://josephthacker.com/favicon-32x32.png","elements":[{"title":"Using Genius AI Models for Important Things: Cheating at NetHack","contents":"<h2 class=\"post-title\">\n      <a href=\"/hacking/2026/08/20/using-genius-hacking-models-for-important-things.html\">\n        Using Genius AI Models for Important Things: Cheating at NetHack\n      </a>\n    </h2>\n    <div class=\"post-meta\">\n  <span class=\"post-date\">20 Aug 2026</span>\n  <span class=\"post-categories\">\n    \n      •\n\n      \n      \n      \n\n      \n        <a href=\"/category/hacking.html\">\n          hacking\n        </a>\n      \n    \n  </span>\n</div>\n\n\n    \n      <p><img src=\"/assets/images/nethack-kraken-farm.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\">\nThis is how I used GPT-5.6 Daybreak Blue to find a buffer overflow, crash the game in order to dupe items, and get the high score on the NetHack 5.0 leaderboard.</p>\n\n\n    \n\n    \n      \n      \n      \n\n      \n        <a href=\"/hacking/2026/08/20/using-genius-hacking-models-for-important-things.html\">More …</a>","link":"https://josephthacker.com/hacking/2026/08/20/using-genius-hacking-models-for-important-things.html","retrieved":1787184000000},{"title":"it's important to say things","contents":"<h2 class=\"post-title\">\n      <a href=\"/personal/2026/07/22/its-important-to-say-things.html\">\n        it's important to say things\n      </a>\n    </h2>\n    <div class=\"post-meta\">\n  <span class=\"post-date\">22 Jul 2026</span>\n  <span class=\"post-categories\">\n    \n      •\n\n      \n      \n      \n\n      \n        <a href=\"/category/personal.html\">\n          personal\n        </a>\n      \n    \n  </span>\n</div>\n\n\n    \n      <p><img src=\"/assets/images/its-important-to-say-things-banner.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\">\n<strong>Ambiguity sucks.</strong> It often leaves people self-conscious. It leaves room for anxiety and doubt. It’s super important to <strong>say things</strong>.</p>\n\n\n    \n\n    \n      \n      \n      \n\n      \n        <a href=\"/personal/2026/07/22/its-important-to-say-things.html\">More …</a>","link":"https://josephthacker.com/personal/2026/07/22/its-important-to-say-things.html","retrieved":1784678400000},{"title":"Launching: rez0's rascals","contents":"<h2 class=\"post-title\">\n      <a href=\"/ai/2026/07/17/launching-rez0s-rascals.html\">\n        Launching: rez0's rascals\n      </a>\n    </h2>\n    <div class=\"post-meta\">\n  <span class=\"post-date\">17 Jul 2026</span>\n  <span class=\"post-categories\">\n    \n      •\n\n      \n      \n      \n\n      \n        <a href=\"/category/ai.html\">\n          ai\n        </a>\n      \n    \n  </span>\n</div>\n\n\n    \n      <p><img src=\"/assets/images/rez0s-rascals-launch.png\" alt=\"Rez0's Rascals\" width=\"600\">\nWhen I launched <a href=\"https://aisafetyforparents.com\">AI Safety For Parents</a>, I said I had built three products and that the other two might surprise you. Here is number two.</p>\n\n\n    \n\n    \n      \n      \n      \n\n      \n        <a href=\"/ai/2026/07/17/launching-rez0s-rascals.html\">More …</a>","link":"https://josephthacker.com/ai/2026/07/17/launching-rez0s-rascals.html","retrieved":1784246400000},{"title":"The Bug Bounty Singularity: Our Hackbot","contents":"<h2 class=\"post-title\">\n      <a href=\"/hacking/2026/07/01/we-built-a-hackbot.html\">\n        The Bug Bounty Singularity: Our Hackbot\n      </a>\n    </h2>\n    <div class=\"post-meta\">\n  <span class=\"post-date\">01 Jul 2026</span>\n  <span class=\"post-categories\">\n    \n      •\n\n      \n      \n      \n\n      \n        <a href=\"/category/hacking.html\">\n          hacking\n        </a>\n      \n    \n  </span>\n</div>\n\n\n    \n      <p><img src=\"/assets/images/hackbot_banner_option_1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"400\">\nThis past December, it became feasible for any skilled hacker to scale up a hacking agent, spending hundreds in token cost to find thousands in bounties. I call this the “Bug Bounty Singularity”. This is the story of JD (<a href=\"https://x.com/xssdoctor\">xssdoctor</a>) and I building a hackbot which found 126 bugs in the last 5 months.</p>\n\n\n    \n\n    \n      \n      \n      \n\n      \n        <a href=\"/hacking/2026/07/01/we-built-a-hackbot.html\">More …</a>","link":"https://josephthacker.com/hacking/2026/07/01/we-built-a-hackbot.html","retrieved":1782864000000},{"title":"Operation Floodlight","contents":"<h2 class=\"post-title\">\n      <a href=\"/hacking/2026/07/01/operation-floodlight.html\">\n        Operation Floodlight\n      </a>\n    </h2>\n    <div class=\"post-meta\">\n  <span class=\"post-date\">01 Jul 2026</span>\n  <span class=\"post-categories\">\n    \n      •\n\n      \n      \n      \n\n      \n        <a href=\"/category/hacking.html\">\n          hacking\n        </a>\n      \n    \n  </span>\n</div>\n\n\n    \n      <p><img src=\"/assets/images/operation_floodlight_banner_candidate_2_clean.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"400\">\nI have been thinking about the downstream impacts of AI systems having strong cybersecurity capabilities.</p>\n\n\n    \n\n    \n      \n      \n      \n\n      \n        <a href=\"/hacking/2026/07/01/operation-floodlight.html\">More …</a>","link":"https://josephthacker.com/hacking/2026/07/01/operation-floodlight.html","retrieved":1782864000000}]}